WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:13.458
Hi! Repeating a name in every sentence sounds clumsy. Pronouns are words that stand for nouns, like he, her and mine. Today we'll learn how to choose the right pronoun.

2
00:00:13.608 --> 00:00:24.570
Before the verb, as the doer, we use a subject pronoun: I, he, they. After a verb or a preposition, we use an object pronoun: me, him, them.

3
00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:33.306
My, your and her need a noun after them: my bag. Mine, yours and hers stand alone with no noun: the bag is mine.

4
00:00:33.456 --> 00:00:45.042
Reflexive pronouns show someone doing something to themselves, or doing it alone. Grandma hurt herself. The twins made the card all by themselves.

5
00:00:45.192 --> 00:00:55.098
When two people are the subject together, cover the other person. I was chosen sounds right, and me was chosen sounds wrong. So it is I, not me.

6
00:00:55.248 --> 00:01:01.482
After the verb gave, we need the person who receives it, so we use the object pronoun me.

7
00:01:01.632 --> 00:01:07.674
Indefinite pronouns like someone, everyone and nobody are singular.

8
00:01:07.824 --> 00:01:13.674
Watch out! Many pupils say: me and Ben went. That's wrong!

9
00:01:13.824 --> 00:01:18.834
Cover Ben: me went to the park sounds wrong. It should be I went.

10
00:01:18.984 --> 00:01:24.762
And it's polite to put yourself last: Ben and I went to the park.

11
00:01:24.912 --> 00:01:36.210
Your turn! This drawing is not, ___. It belongs to Sally. My, mine or me? Pause and think.

12
00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:43.458
Mine. There is no noun after it, so we use mine. Did you get it right?

13
00:01:43.608 --> 00:01:53.802
Another one! The twins made the card all by, ___. Which pronoun? Pause and think.

14
00:01:53.952 --> 00:02:01.722
Themselves. By themselves means they did it alone, with no help. Did you get it right?

15
00:02:01.872 --> 00:02:12.186
Next one! Mrs Lee gave, ___, a sticker. I, me or my? Pause and think.

16
00:02:12.336 --> 00:02:22.530
Me. It comes after the verb gave, and it is the person who gets the sticker, so we need the object pronoun. Did you get it right?

17
00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:33.450
One more! Grandma hurt, ___, when she fell. Her, hers or herself? Pause and think.

18
00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:41.898
Herself. Grandma hurt her own body, so we use the reflexive pronoun. Did you get it right?

19
00:02:42.048 --> 00:02:51.978
Last one! Is this umbrella, ___, Ben? Your, yours or you? Pause and think.

20
00:02:52.128 --> 00:02:59.178
Yours. No noun follows it, so we use yours. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:59.328 --> 00:03:08.226
Remember: before the verb, as the subject, use I, he or they. After a verb or preposition, use me, him or them.

22
00:03:08.376 --> 00:03:17.202
Use my or her before a noun, and mine or hers on their own. Use myself or themselves for doing something to yourself, or alone.

23
00:03:17.352 --> 00:03:22.890
When you talk with your family, notice which pronouns you use!

